# Ignore everything
*

# But descend into directories
!*/

# Whitelist files
!*.sh
!*.py
!*.c
!*.cpp
!*.h
!*.hpp
!*.json
!*.md
!.gitignore

# Ignore build/output directories even if they match above rules (if they contain allowed files but we want to ignore the folder itself, though !*/ usually allows them. Specific ignore might be needed if !*/ is too broad but usually okay)
# Actually, if we !*/, git looks inside. If inside is build output like .o files, they are ignored by *.
# If binary has no extension, it is ignored by *.
# If binary is named 'pointer_analysis', it is ignored.
# This seems correct for user request.
